## Validate the Ubuntu Runtime Matrix

For the VersatusHPC Ubuntu release candidate, run the maintained runtime gate
from a source checkout after the cluster is installed. Do not run this script
through SSH standard input; package-manager commands may consume stdin.

```bash
scp scripts/validate-ubuntu-runtime.sh <sms-host>:/tmp/
ssh <sms-host> \
  'chmod +x /tmp/validate-ubuntu-runtime.sh &&
   /tmp/validate-ubuntu-runtime.sh --install-intel'
```

The `--install-intel` gate checks public APT package candidates, Slurm,
Warewulf compute-node state, MUNGE, PMIx/HWLOC linker visibility, the OpenHPC
Yama policy, GNU15 with OpenMPI/MPICH/MVAPICH2/Intel MPI, Intel with Intel
MPI/OpenMPI/MPICH/MVAPICH2, and IMB `PingPong` for the same matrix. Use
`--skip-intel` on systems where Intel oneAPI validation is intentionally out of
scope.
